  "body": "Stacked on #3880 (merge #3880 first).\n\n## What changed\n\n- `crates/motion/src/machining3d/ladder.rs`: a pass that restarts after a hop with a straight plunge now calls `descent::feed_down`. The tool goes down by a rapid to the plunge height over the material. Then it feeds the rest. Before, it fed the whole way from the hop plane.\n- `crates/motion/src/machining3d/descent.rs`: `feed_down` is now `pub(super)`. The code does not change.\n- `crates/motion/src/machining3d/short_moves.rs` (new): `merge_short_feeds` merges each straight feed that moves less than 0.001 mm on every axis into its straight neighbour. A short move with no straight feed beside it stays. The chain of moves stays unbroken. `ladder` calls it on the finished path when the path has no compensation spans.\n- `examples/catalog/3d/rough-finish`: made again with `cargo xtask catalog --case 3d/rough-finish`.\n- `docs/decisions/3852-pocket-restart-rapid.md`: the choices and what was dropped.\n\n## Cause\n\n1. The restart branch in `ladder` pushed a rapid to the hop plane and then one plunge to the level. It did not use the plunge-height rapid that the level entry uses.\n2. Offset-ring vertices that are almost the same point gave feed moves shorter than 0.001 mm. The post wrote them as `G01` blocks with the same X, Y and Z as the block before them.\n\nNote: after #3857 (ea39d4180), the catalog case posts no restart plunge. Its restarts take the ramp. The straight-plunge branch is still reached when the entry is Plunge, or when no entry fits. The motion pin uses that path.\n\n## Tests\n\nPins:\n\n- `camcraft-motion` `pocket3d_pass_start::zigzag_plunge_restarts_feed_only_from_the_plunge_height`. A Plunge-entry zigzag around an island, two levels. No plunge is longer than the plunge height plus the stepdown.\n  - Red before the fix: `Zigzag: a plunge of 13.5 mm feeds from the hop plane: Move { kind: Plunge, from: Point3 { x: 26.828135, y: 12.61, z: 20.0 }, to: ... z: 6.5 }`.\n- `camcraft-app` `example_catalog` `catalog_3d_rough_finish::pocket_posts_no_hop_plane_plunge_and_no_zero_length_move`. It reads the posted 3D Pocket section of `rough-finish.nc` (the \"Done when\" of the issue).\n  - Red before the fix: `18 zero-length moves posted: [\"G01 X-10.417 Y-6.883 Z17.367 F1200.\", ...]`.\n- `camcraft-motion` lib `machining3d::short_moves::tests` (5 unit tests): join into the next feed, join into the previous feed before a rapid, a run of short feeds, no join into a plunge or an arc, a 0.001 mm move stays.\n\nMutations:\n\n- Put back the old straight plunge in `ladder`: the motion pin is red (the same 13.5 mm message). Restored: green.\n- Turn off the `merge_short_feeds` call: `catalog_3d_rough_finish::regenerates` is red. After `cargo xtask catalog --case 3d/rough-finish`, the catalog pin is red (18 zero-length moves). Restored: all 6 `catalog_3d_rough_finish` tests are green.\n\nGate (on code head b3a68d63d; the last commit adds only the decision file):\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: 51 steps, 0 failed.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- `example_catalog`, `example_catalog_adaptive`, `example_catalog_edge_work`: all green (43 + 1 + 1 passed).\n- `cargo xtask gate light --base upstream/main`: 6 steps, 0 failed.\n- Heavy lanes: not run. The dry run reaches 104 release steps. AGENTS.md \"Heavy lanes at review\" (#3556) gives a P7 PR no heavy step. The cut gate runs them.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\n- `examples/catalog/3d/rough-finish/rough-finish.nc`: 28 lines removed, 0 added, all in the 3D Pocket section. Each removed `G01` block is within 0.001 mm on each axis of the block before it. 18 of them were exact duplicates. 10 differed by one count of the last digit (for example `X-10.448 Y-6.835` after `X-10.447 Y-6.835`). The 3D Finish sections do not change.\n- `examples/catalog/3d/rough-finish/rough-finish.camproj`: the cached toolpath of the 3D Pocket, made again by the same tool.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No machine run. The program was read, not cut.\n- The merge applies to the 3D Pocket ladder only. Other generators can still post sub-resolution moves.\n- `ladder.rs` was 444 lines on the base. It is 446 lines now. A split is not in this PR.\n\n## Overlaps\n\n- Stacked on #3880: it changes the same restart block in `ladder` (the `again` Ask) and `descent::from`.\n- #3869 changes `ladder` too (the level target query, other lines). It also makes `rough-finish.nc` again. The PR that merges second makes the catalog case again.\n\nChangelog: 3D Pocket: a pass restart with a straight plunge now rapids to the plunge height over the material before it feeds, and feed moves shorter than 0.001 mm no longer post as zero-length G01 blocks.\n\nFixes #3852\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
